  "modified": "2026-10-01T08:56:03Z",
  "details": "- CVE-2026-96808: the revokefs writer validated the paths its unprivileged\n  client sends with validate_path()/get_valid_path(), which rejected literal\n  \"..\" components but followed symlinks, so a local user holding two revokefs\n  sessions could make one session write through a symlink into the other and\n  tamper with ostree objects after flatpak-system-helper had verified them;\n  the request handlers now resolve the parent directory with\n  glnx_chaseat(GLNX_CHASE_RESOLVE_BENEATH) through the new chase_parent(),\n  chase_request_path(), chase_request_2path() and chase_request_any_and_path()\n  helpers and act on the final component with *at() syscalls confined beneath\n  basefd",
